1
00:02:00,472 --> 00:02:02,365
 اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:02:03,913 --> 00:02:05,457
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:02:06,528 --> 00:02:08,695
 اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد

4
00:02:09,394 --> 00:02:11,349
 وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسليمًا كثيرا

5
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:15,756
The virtues of a Ash-Shuhadaa(ألشُهَدآء).

6
00:02:17,365 --> 00:02:20,292
Ash-Shuhadaa(ألشُهَدآء) are blessed with many virtues from Allah,

7
00:02:20,462 --> 00:02:21,496
some of which are,

8
00:02:23,391 --> 00:02:26,516
and Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) I think mentions, how many does he mention?

9
00:02:27,636 --> 00:02:28,849
Are they 19!

10
00:02:32,246 --> 00:02:37,328
He has actually nine. Nine virtues!

11
00:02:41,318 --> 00:02:45,688
The first one is to desire to die again for the sake of Allah.

12
00:02:49,828 --> 00:02:58,721
No one; who enters paradise wants to leave it, even if they are given the world and everything on it,

13
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:01,558
 with the exception of the Shaheed(شَهِيد).

14
00:03:03,689 --> 00:03:08,170
He wants to leave paradise come back to this world and be killed in the sake of Allah again.

15
00:03:08,645 --> 00:03:10,876
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم), the Messenger of Allah says;

16
00:03:11,297 --> 00:03:15,170
No one, who enters paradise would want to go back to Earth but the Shaheed(شَهِيد),

17
00:03:15,583 --> 00:03:19,480
he wants to go back to Earth in order to be killed for the sake of Allah 10 times.

18
00:03:20,057 --> 00:03:23,556
That is when he sees what Allah has reserved for the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

19
00:03:24,136 --> 00:03:27,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ himself says in the name of whom Muhammad(محمد) soul in His hand,

20
00:03:28,301 --> 00:03:31,333
I wish I could fight in the cause of Allah and then be killed,

21
00:03:31,413 --> 00:03:34,502
and then fight and then be killed and then fight and then be killed.

22
00:03:36,422 --> 00:03:42,271
Number two, forgiveness of all sins,

23
00:03:43,539 --> 00:03:49,105
the moment the soul of the Shaheed(شَهِيد) leaves his body, it also leaves all his sins behind.

24
00:03:49,941 --> 00:03:51,932
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم) Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة) said:

25
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:55,043
Rasool Allah ﷺ delivered a Khut'ba(خطبة) and he said:

26
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,162
The Jihad(جهاد) in the path of Allah and Eeman(ايمان) are the greatest of all deeds.

27
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,450
 So a man stood up and said:

28
00:04:01,728 --> 00:04:06,323
O Rasool Ullah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, will that forgive my sins?

29
00:04:06,935 --> 00:04:12,680
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes, if you die with steadfastness and sincerity,

30
00:04:13,046 --> 00:04:16,502
 facing your enemy, and not turning your back to him.

31
00:04:16,823 --> 00:04:18,047
The man asked again,

32
00:04:18,373 --> 00:04:20,053
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

33
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:25,760
 If you die was steadfastness and sincerity, facing your enemy and not turning your back to him.

34
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:27,870
And if you are not in debt.

35
00:04:28,361 --> 00:04:29,969
مُقْبِلٌ غَيْرُ مُدْبِرٍ

36
00:04:31,265 --> 00:04:32,889
 Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) told me that.

37
00:04:33,541 --> 00:04:36,212
So, the exception here is debt.

38
00:04:37,957 --> 00:04:40,075
 Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Al-Aas(عبدالله بن عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) narrated,

39
00:04:40,092 --> 00:04:43,052
The Messenger of Allah said: The Shaheed(شَهِيد) is forgiven everything except debt

40
00:04:43,124 --> 00:04:44,946
 and this is in Muslim(ألمسلم) and In Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم) And Ahmad(أحمد).

41
00:04:45,384 --> 00:04:48,717
So what does Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) say about debt?

42
00:04:49,797 --> 00:04:51,183
 Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says:

43
00:04:52,111 --> 00:04:59,480
the debt that is intended here, is when the Shaheed(شَهِيد) had the capability of paying it back,

44
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:04,566
but didn't or have the option of writing it in his will, and he didn't.

45
00:05:05,284 --> 00:05:09,999
It would also include money that was borrowed for wasteful reason, and was not returned.

46
00:05:10,634 --> 00:05:13,800
But when the Shaheed(شَهِيد) borrows money due to poverty and dire need,

47
00:05:13,957 --> 00:05:16,346
 and is then incapable of paying it back,

48
00:05:16,806 --> 00:05:19,187
this would not withhold the Shaheed(شَهِيد) from Paradise.

49
00:05:19,751 --> 00:05:22,189
In this case, the Sultan(سلطان) should pay back his debt,

50
00:05:22,721 --> 00:05:26,013
if that didn't happen, then Allah Himself will pay it back for him.

51
00:05:26,487 --> 00:05:27,757
As a Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

52
00:05:27,774 --> 00:05:32,467
When you borrow and you sincerely want to pay it back, Allah will pay it for you.

53
00:05:33,156 --> 00:05:36,094
And when you borrow money to waste, Allah will waste it.

54
00:05:36,531 --> 00:05:37,471
 And that's in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

55
00:05:37,876 --> 00:05:39,931
So this point should be clear about debt.

56
00:05:40,781 --> 00:05:45,956
If a person was in need, serious need, and they borrowed money they went to on Jihad(جهاد).

57
00:05:46,685 --> 00:05:48,534
They couldn't pay it back before they go,

58
00:05:49,003 --> 00:05:51,161
and they ended up dying Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

59
00:05:51,590 --> 00:05:53,346
that's not gonna withhold them from Jannah(جنة).

60
00:05:53,806 --> 00:05:57,543
 But if somebody had enough money to buy a Honda Accord,

61
00:05:57,893 --> 00:06:02,085
 nevertheless, they wanted to buy a brand new BMW, and they borrowed money for that.

62
00:06:02,668 --> 00:06:03,862
 And they didn't pay it back.

63
00:06:04,133 --> 00:06:07,762
That's a debt, that's unforgiving because, it's for a wasteful reason.

64
00:06:08,699 --> 00:06:09,912
The Messenger of Allah said:

65
00:06:10,818 --> 00:06:14,103
The Shaheed(شَهِيد) has seven qualities,

66
00:06:14,543 --> 00:06:18,242
he would be forgiven with the first drop of his blood.

67
00:06:18,663 --> 00:06:23,824
So just imagine that on the first drop of blood makes a touchdown,

68
00:06:24,729 --> 00:06:26,021
 all of the sins are gone,

69
00:06:29,386 --> 00:06:30,592
Ahmad(أحمد) and Tabrani(طبراني).

70
00:06:31,826 --> 00:06:33,493
Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Al-Aas(عبدالله بن عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said:

71
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:36,120
When the servant is killed in the cause of Allah,

72
00:06:36,517 --> 00:06:42,773
as soon as the first drop of his blood touches the ground, all of his sins are forgiven.

73
00:06:43,458 --> 00:06:44,241
Number three,

74
00:06:45,955 --> 00:06:49,580
the angels provide shade for the Shaheed(شَهِيد) with their wings.

75
00:06:49,843 --> 00:06:54,364
Now, Allah Alam(ألله أعلم) if this, Yani(يعني) I believe that this is specific,

76
00:06:54,618 --> 00:06:58,459
even though Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) mentioned it as something for all of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء)

77
00:06:58,817 --> 00:07:01,040
but it might be specific to this particular case.

78
00:07:01,477 --> 00:07:06,451
Jabir(جابر) narrated that his father was presented to the Messenger of Allah after his dead body was mutilated.

79
00:07:06,891 --> 00:07:09,874
I wanted to uncover his face but some people told me not to.

80
00:07:10,311 --> 00:07:12,840
 We then heard some woman weeping so Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

81
00:07:12,873 --> 00:07:13,873
 Why are you weeping?

82
00:07:14,238 --> 00:07:18,398
The angels are still providing shade for him up to this moment,

83
00:07:18,793 --> 00:07:24,842
Allah Alam(ألله أعلم), this might be a special honor to the father of Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله).

84
00:07:26,283 --> 00:07:30,298
Number four martyrdom, guarantees paradise.

85
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:31,497
Allah says:

86
00:07:31,621 --> 00:07:39,318
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم

87
00:07:39,619 --> 00:07:44,706
وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

88
00:07:44,952 --> 00:07:51,977
يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَيَقتُلونَ وَيُقتَلونَ

89
00:07:52,351 --> 00:08:00,446
ۖ وَعدًا عَلَيهِ حَقًّا فِي التَّوراةِ وَالإِنجيلِ وَالقُرآنِ

90
00:08:00,741 --> 00:08:05,255
ۚ وَمَن أَوفىٰ بِعَهدِهِ مِنَ اللَّهِ

91
00:08:05,407 --> 00:08:11,067
 ۚ فَاستَبشِروا بِبَيعِكُمُ الَّذي بايَعتُم بِهِ

92
00:08:11,163 --> 00:08:15,596
ۚ وَذٰلِكَ هُوَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

93
00:08:15,757 --> 00:08:18,297
Indeed Allah has purchased from the believers, their lives

94
00:08:18,678 --> 00:08:22,032
and their properties and in exchange for that they will have paradise,

95
00:08:22,156 --> 00:08:23,194
At-Toba(التوبة) Verse 111.

96
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:25,686
And Allah also says,

97
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:38,020
فَإِذا لَقيتُمُ الَّذينَ كَفَروا فَضَربَ الرِّقابِ حَتّىٰ إِذا أَثخَنتُموهُم فَشُدُّوا الوَثاقَ

98
00:08:38,549 --> 00:08:48,092
فَإِمّا مَنًّا بَعدُ وَإِمّا فِداءً حَتّىٰ تَضَعَ الحَربُ أَوزارَها ۚ

99
00:08:48,621 --> 00:08:54,275
ذٰلِكَ وَلَو يَشاءُ اللَّهُ لَانتَصَرَ مِنهُم

100
00:08:54,526 --> 00:08:58,245
وَلٰكِن لِيَبلُوَ بَعضَكُم بِبَعضٍۗ

101
00:08:58,535 --> 00:09:05,102
وَالَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَلَن يُضِلَّ أَعمالَهُم۞

102
00:09:05,468 --> 00:09:08,723
سَيَهديهِم وَيُصلِحُ بالَهُم ۞

103
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:13,777
وَيُدخِلُهُمُ الجَنَّةَ عَرَّفَها لَهُم ۞

104
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:16,652
And those who are killed in the cause of Allah.

105
00:09:17,081 --> 00:09:18,985
Never will He waste their deeds.

106
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:22,858
He will guide them and amend their condition and admit them to paradise.

107
00:09:23,089 --> 00:09:24,950
 Muhammad(محمد), Verse four to six.

108
00:09:25,468 --> 00:09:27,897
Samura Bin Jundab(سمرة بن جندب) narrated,

109
00:09:27,977 --> 00:09:29,191
the Messenger of Allah said:

110
00:09:29,573 --> 00:09:34,169
I've dreamed last night of two men who ascended with me and took me up to a tree

111
00:09:35,017 --> 00:09:38,612
and we entered the mansion, I've never seen anything more beautiful than it.

112
00:09:39,278 --> 00:09:42,025
They said: This mansion is for the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

113
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:47,445
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

114
00:09:48,366 --> 00:09:49,675
Allah laughs at two men,

115
00:09:50,335 --> 00:09:53,601
 one of them kills the other and they both enter into paradise.

116
00:09:54,237 --> 00:09:56,811
They said: How can that happen, O Messenger of Allah?

117
00:09:57,153 --> 00:09:58,871
 he said: One of them kills the other.

118
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:02,047
So the one who is killed goes to paradise, as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

119
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:04,532
And then the one who killed him, embraces Islam

120
00:10:05,031 --> 00:10:09,623
goes and fight in the path of Allah and is killed as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) and goes to paradise.

121
00:10:12,476 --> 00:10:20,003
There's another Hadith(حديث) that when a Kafir(كافر) kills a Muslim,

122
00:10:21,504 --> 00:10:23,423
and then that Kafir(كافر) and becomes a Muslim,

123
00:10:24,122 --> 00:10:27,010
 these two men end up loving each other so much in Jannah(جنة).

124
00:10:28,257 --> 00:10:30,947
Because the Muslim knows that I got here because of you.

125
00:10:32,378 --> 00:10:36,140
And the Kafir(كافر) says Al-hamdulillah(ألحمدلله) that guided me to Islam.

126
00:10:36,196 --> 00:10:39,652
So, they end up having that close bond in Jannah(جنة).

127
00:10:45,057 --> 00:10:49,581
 Anas(أنس) narrated, the mother of Harisa(حارثه) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and asked him:

128
00:10:49,663 --> 00:10:52,787
O messenger of Allah! Won't you tell me about my son Harisa(حارثه),

129
00:10:53,631 --> 00:10:58,430
 if he is in paradise I would be patient and if he is not I would cry for him.

130
00:10:59,311 --> 00:11:03,281
Harisa(حارثه) was killed during the Battle of Badr(بدر) by stray arrow, in a friendly fire.

131
00:11:03,614 --> 00:11:05,324
 So that's why his mother was worried.

132
00:11:05,984 --> 00:11:08,578
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Have you lost your mind.

133
00:11:08,633 --> 00:11:09,294
أهابلتي

134
00:11:09,825 --> 00:11:14,870
It is not one paradise, but many, and your son is in the highest one, Al-firdaus(ألفردوس).

135
00:11:16,458 --> 00:11:17,426
Number five,

136
00:11:18,688 --> 00:11:21,764
Their souls are in the inside of green birds in paradise.

137
00:11:22,927 --> 00:11:25,453
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) narrated, the Messenger of Allah said:

138
00:11:26,215 --> 00:11:27,897
When your brothers were killed at Uhud(أحَد),

139
00:11:28,128 --> 00:11:33,140
Allah had their souls in the insides of green birds,

140
00:11:33,545 --> 00:11:39,461
 flying on the banks of the rivers of Paradise, and eating from the fruits thereof.

141
00:11:40,216 --> 00:11:45,062
At night, these birds spend their evening in lanterns hanging to the throne of Allah.

142
00:11:45,841 --> 00:11:50,291
So during the day, taking a tour of the rivers of Paradise,

143
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:56,649
the best beaches you could dream of, accrues on these beaches,

144
00:11:56,746 --> 00:11:59,205
 and then they spend the night under the throne of Allah.

145
00:12:00,713 --> 00:12:03,591
When the martyrs saw the blessings they were in, they said,

146
00:12:03,703 --> 00:12:07,282
 who would convey to our brothers that we are living in Paradise,

147
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:09,732
 so they won't ignore Jihad(جهاد) and stop fighting,

148
00:12:10,407 --> 00:12:11,586
Allah than revealed.

149
00:12:11,685 --> 00:12:18,469
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ

150
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:23,448
بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

151
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:29,790
So the whole purpose of the revelation of this Ayah(آية) was to fulfill the desire of these Shuhadaa(شهداء)

152
00:12:29,876 --> 00:12:32,990
because people did not know yet that the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) were alive,

153
00:12:33,047 --> 00:12:35,144
they did not know yet what the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) were going through.

154
00:12:35,192 --> 00:12:41,083
So these Sahabah(صحابه) they wanted their brothers to know about what's happening.

155
00:12:42,572 --> 00:12:47,758
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed  the Ayaat(آيات) of Al-Imran(ألعمران), and Al-Baqarah(ألبقرة), which is talking about Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

156
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:54,524
And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead

157
00:12:54,563 --> 00:12:58,032
 rather they are alive with their Lord receiving provisions.

158
00:12:58,342 --> 00:13:01,173
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ

159
00:13:01,634 --> 00:13:04,229
بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

160
00:13:05,063 --> 00:13:08,038
Rejoicing what Allah has bestowed on them of His bounty,

161
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:11,575
and they receive good tidings about those after them,

162
00:13:11,917 --> 00:13:19,431
 who have not yet joined them, that there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.

163
00:13:20,753 --> 00:13:25,044
They receive good tidings of favor from Allah and bounty

164
00:13:25,181 --> 00:13:28,805
 and that Allah does not allow the reward of the believers to be lost.

165
00:13:31,058 --> 00:13:33,174
And this is in Abu Daud(أبوداؤد) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

166
00:13:33,968 --> 00:13:34,761
 Number six,

167
00:13:35,306 --> 00:13:37,639
They are not punished in their graves.

168
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:41,460
There is a Hadith(حديث) that states that the one who dies in Ribat(رباط)

169
00:13:41,492 --> 00:13:43,269
 would not be tested in their graves.

170
00:13:43,286 --> 00:13:45,412
If this occurs to the one who dies in Ribat(رباط).

171
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,533
Then what about the one who dies as the Shaheed(شَهِيد).

172
00:13:48,335 --> 00:13:51,633
 The interrogation of the grave is meant to test the faith of a person.

173
00:13:52,175 --> 00:13:54,968
Now if the Shaheed(شَهِيد) died fighting for the sake of Allah,

174
00:13:55,254 --> 00:13:59,752
with swords flashing above his head, spears and arrows flying next to him,

175
00:14:00,269 --> 00:14:03,002
 and seeing heads and limbs being chopped off,

176
00:14:03,636 --> 00:14:08,166
whoever sees that and then doesn't retreat, but rather fights until they die.

177
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:12,368
Giving up their soul for Allah is enough as a test for his faith.

178
00:14:14,476 --> 00:14:19,482
So now you can replace the swords, spears and arrows with fire.

179
00:14:21,447 --> 00:14:21,993
 Number seven,

180
00:14:22,526 --> 00:14:25,990
The Shaheed(شَهِيد) is spared from the shock of the blow of the horn.

181
00:14:28,017 --> 00:14:29,746
Saeed Ibn Jubair(سعيد إبن جبير) was asked:

182
00:14:29,794 --> 00:14:33,277
Who are the ones excluded by Allah  the following verse

183
00:14:34,817 --> 00:14:42,283
and the horn will be blown and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth will fall dead except whom Allah wills.

184
00:14:44,361 --> 00:14:45,971
He said: They are the martyrs,

185
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:51,995
everyone else dies while they are surrounding the throne of Allah with their swords in their hands.

186
00:14:52,938 --> 00:14:55,838
Now there's different views on who these are,

187
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:57,303
إلَّا ما شاء ربك

188
00:14:57,362 --> 00:14:59,586
The ones who are excluded from this Ayah(آية).

189
00:15:01,729 --> 00:15:03,822
Some say it's talking about Al-Malaikah(ألملائكة).

190
00:15:03,831 --> 00:15:08,161
Some say it's talking about Al-Hoor Al-Ain(ألحورالعين) in Jannah(جنة).

191
00:15:08,897 --> 00:15:13,393
And then you have this opinion here that it's a Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء), they are alive.

192
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:17,472
 And this is in Ibn Al-Mubarik(أبن المبارك), Bukhari(بخاريْ) in Al-Kabir(ألكبير),

193
00:15:17,735 --> 00:15:20,450
Abu Naeem(أبونعيم) At-Tabari(ألطبري) in his Tafseer(تفسير).

194
00:15:20,475 --> 00:15:25,436
As-Sayuti(ألسيوطي) says it's authentic and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم)  narrates it and Az-Zahbi(ألذهبي) authenticates it.

195
00:15:26,755 --> 00:15:30,993
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) about the ones who are excluded from the shock of the horn,

196
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:31,796
 Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said:

197
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:32,435
They are the martyrs,

198
00:15:32,674 --> 00:15:33,451
Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

199
00:15:37,091 --> 00:15:37,962
Number eight:

200
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:45,683
that's the mistake that should be number eight, that's Number 8

201
00:15:47,102 --> 00:15:50,813
The Shaheed(شَهِيد) intercedes for 70 of his family.

202
00:15:52,292 --> 00:15:56,628
Noman Bin Ut'ba(نعمان بن عُتْبَة) said: We went to visit on Um-Darda(أم درداء), and we were orphans

203
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,212
 she said, rejoice.

204
00:15:59,067 --> 00:16:02,551
I heard my husband Abu Darda(أبودرداء) say: Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

205
00:16:02,877 --> 00:16:06,597
 The Shaheed(شَهِيد) will intercede on behalf of 70 of his relatives.

206
00:16:07,192 --> 00:16:09,501
Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Ibn Haban(إبن حبان) and Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي).

207
00:16:10,113 --> 00:16:13,441
Now, this does not include friends, Is that clear?

208
00:16:13,461 --> 00:16:16,981
 It's just for family, this is for family not friends.

209
00:16:18,199 --> 00:16:20,888
So we can only intercede for your family.

210
00:16:22,799 --> 00:16:25,622
Your wives, your children, your parents, relatives.

211
00:16:27,688 --> 00:16:28,695
Number 10:

212
00:16:29,842 --> 00:16:32,779
The Shaheed(شَهِيد) feels peace on the Day of Judgment.

213
00:16:34,837 --> 00:16:39,888
Nine, sorry. The Shaheed(شَهِيد) feels peace on the Day of Judgment.

214
00:16:41,087 --> 00:16:47,367
Rasool Allah ﷺ said and he, the Shaheed(شَهِيد) feels peace at the time of the greatest fear.

215
00:16:48,664 --> 00:16:50,776
Do you know, with the fear of the Day of Judgment.

216
00:16:52,226 --> 00:16:55,430
 It's so horrific.

217
00:16:56,629 --> 00:16:58,271
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says about it,

218
00:16:58,295 --> 00:17:00,549
يومًا يجعل الولدان شيبا

219
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:05,965
It's a day that will make the child, gray headed.

220
00:17:10,098 --> 00:17:12,952
 And we recited the Ayah(آية) from Surat Ul Hajj(سورة الحَجْ),

221
00:17:13,016 --> 00:17:24,551
يا أَيُّهَا النّاسُ اتَّقوا رَبَّكُم ۚ إِنَّ زَلزَلَةَ السّاعَةِ شَيءٌ عَظيمٌ۞

222
00:17:25,099 --> 00:17:37,895
يَومَ تَرَونَها تَذهَلُ كُلُّ مُرضِعَةٍ عَمّا أَرضَعَت وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها

223
00:17:38,728 --> 00:17:48,749
وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها وَتَرَى النّاسَ سُكارىٰ وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ

224
00:17:49,277 --> 00:17:56,919
وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ وَلٰكِنَّ عَذابَ اللَّهِ شَديدٌ۞

225
00:17:57,293 --> 00:17:59,893
إِنَّ زَلزَلَةَ السّاعَةِ شَيءٌ عَظيمٌ۞

226
00:18:00,835 --> 00:18:05,443
That the shaking and the trials of the Day of Judgment is a huge affair.

227
00:18:05,734 --> 00:18:11,888
يَومَ تَرَونَها تَذهَلُ كُلُّ مُرضِعَةٍ عَمّا أَرضَعَت وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها

228
00:18:12,222 --> 00:18:15,776
 وَتَرَى النّاسَ سُكارىٰ وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ وَلٰكِنَّ عَذابَ اللَّهِ شَديدٌ۞

229
00:18:18,092 --> 00:18:24,423
The pregnant woman would have a miscarriage and you see people as if they're drunk,

230
00:18:25,051 --> 00:18:26,114
 but they're not drunk.

231
00:18:26,908 --> 00:18:29,575
It is because of the terror of that day.

232
00:18:31,011 --> 00:18:34,957
 Now for Shaheed(شَهِيد) to be safe on that day,

233
00:18:36,275 --> 00:18:40,819
for the Shaheed(شَهِيد) it was a few minutes and then he lost his soul.

234
00:18:42,245 --> 00:18:48,498
 And the result would be feeling safe on the Day of Judgment, which is 50,000 years long.

235
00:18:50,273 --> 00:18:52,775
 You see the Bedouin was very wise when he made the Dua(دُعَا).

236
00:18:53,678 --> 00:19:06,703
اللهم اجعل خير أعمالنا خواتمها ، وخير أعمارنا أواخرها ، وخير أيامنا يوم ألقاك فيه،

237
00:19:07,597 --> 00:19:09,834
There is a Bedouin who made the Dua(دُعَا), he said: Oh Allah!

238
00:19:10,906 --> 00:19:14,272
 I asked you to make the best of my deeds the last one.

239
00:19:15,225 --> 00:19:17,470
And the best of my life, the end of it.

240
00:19:18,090 --> 00:19:20,224
And the best of my day, is the day of judgment.

241
00:19:20,447 --> 00:19:21,272
 The day when I meet You.

242
00:19:22,157 --> 00:19:26,293
See if you want to have the best day in your life, make sure that is the day of judgment

243
00:19:27,150 --> 00:19:32,102
because that day is longer than your entire life in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) multiplied by a 1000.

244
00:19:35,977 --> 00:19:38,389
So, for a Shaheed(شَهِيد) to have peace on that day

245
00:19:38,399 --> 00:19:42,635
and you know having peace on that day is such an important thing

246
00:19:42,652 --> 00:19:46,586
that the Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ mentioned that this was Dua(دُعَا) of Eesa عليه السّلام.

247
00:19:48,118 --> 00:20:00,574
وَالسَّلامُ عَلَيَّ يَومَ وُلِدتُ وَيَومَ أَموتُ وَيَومَ أُبعَثُ حَيًّا۞

248
00:20:01,389 --> 00:20:06,297
Peace on them today was born the day he dies and the day is brought up again, which is the day of judgment.

249
00:20:18,656 --> 00:20:21,118
The next one would be number 10.

250
00:20:22,001 --> 00:20:27,270
The blood of the Shaheed(شَهِيد) doesn't dry until he sees his wives in paradise.

251
00:20:28,584 --> 00:20:32,552
 Abdullah Bin Obaidellah Bin Umair(عبدالله بن عبيدالله بن عمير) said:

252
00:20:32,897 --> 00:20:34,321
When the two armies meet,

253
00:20:34,798 --> 00:20:38,930
the women of Paradise descend to the lower heaven to watch the battle.

254
00:20:40,827 --> 00:20:42,128
 Halal(حلال) cheerleaders.

255
00:20:43,485 --> 00:20:44,949
If they see a man steadfast,

256
00:20:44,998 --> 00:20:48,116
they say: Oh, Allah him confirm.

257
00:20:48,945 --> 00:20:51,959
While if he turns his back, they turn away from him.

258
00:20:52,878 --> 00:20:53,678
 So Yani(يعني),

259
00:20:53,702 --> 00:20:57,081
if he's running away, they actually don't want to see that, he turn away.

260
00:20:58,344 --> 00:21:02,952
If he is killed, they come down to him and wipe the dirt from his face.

261
00:21:03,795 --> 00:21:07,112
That's Sahih(صحيح) narrated by Abdur Razzaq(عبدالرزاق).

262
00:21:09,945 --> 00:21:17,917
In fact, it is quite a Mutawatir(متواتر) reference that

263
00:21:18,103 --> 00:21:22,744
some Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) not only see it when they're dying, but sometimes they see it even before that.

264
00:21:24,204 --> 00:21:30,819
A brother was telling of, people whom he knows firsthand, and this is in Iraq,

265
00:21:34,686 --> 00:21:37,009
in the North, Kurds.

266
00:21:39,110 --> 00:21:46,959
The brother was sitting with, with his friends, and his eyes were fixed on something in front of him.

267
00:21:48,501 --> 00:21:51,179
So the brothers were talking to him and he's not responding,

268
00:21:51,203 --> 00:21:54,750
and they're trying to get his attention and he just his eyes are fixed.

269
00:21:55,568 --> 00:21:58,355
 And then after that, he sort of woke up he was daydreaming

270
00:21:58,386 --> 00:22:00,095
 and they asked him what's happening.?

271
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:04,877
He said: I was seeing in front of me, woman of Jannah(جنة), I was seeing Hur(حور) in front of me.

272
00:22:06,093 --> 00:22:09,375
After he said that the missile landed right there and killed no one but him.

273
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:15,936
But it happened but he saw the Hur(حور) before he actually was going through the death process.

274
00:22:16,032 --> 00:22:19,872
It was while he was still, Yani(يعني) nothing was happening.

275
00:22:19,897 --> 00:22:22,463
And he was seeing the Hur(حور) when he was still awake.

276
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:25,035
This wasn't a dream, it was daydreaming.

277
00:22:26,509 --> 00:22:30,058
So this is a contemporary story, and there are plenty of other stories in Afghanistan

278
00:22:30,091 --> 00:22:31,781
all over you must have heard, many of them.

279
00:22:32,948 --> 00:22:37,872
Of people actually seeing Al-Hur(ألحور) well in advance.

280
00:22:43,647 --> 00:22:45,998
What number are we? Eleven,11.

281
00:22:47,246 --> 00:22:53,143
The one who dies as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) is better than the one who wins and returns home safely.

282
00:22:54,367 --> 00:22:57,960
Jabir(جابر) narrates the Messenger of Allah was asked about the best Jihad(جهاد).

283
00:22:58,333 --> 00:22:58,927
He said;

284
00:22:59,489 --> 00:23:04,857
The best Jihad(جهاد) is the one in which your horse is slain, and your blood is spilled.

285
00:23:05,587 --> 00:23:07,982
I mention this Hadith(حديث) a few times before.

286
00:23:08,434 --> 00:23:11,203
Amr Bin Absa(عمرو بن عبسة) narrates a man said:

287
00:23:11,244 --> 00:23:13,028
O Messenger of Allah! What is Islam?

288
00:23:14,148 --> 00:23:20,035
He said: Islam is the submission of your heart and that the Muslims are safe from your tongue and your hands.

289
00:23:20,109 --> 00:23:21,655
 He said: What is the best of Islam?

290
00:23:21,981 --> 00:23:23,726
Rasool Allah ﷺ Eeman(ايمان).

291
00:23:23,909 --> 00:23:25,102
He said: What is the Eeman(ايمان)?

292
00:23:25,333 --> 00:23:29,963
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers,

293
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,947
and the resurrection after death.

294
00:23:32,026 --> 00:23:33,680
He said: What is the best of Eeman(ايمان)?

295
00:23:33,746 --> 00:23:34,804
Rasool Allah ﷺ said Hijrah(هجرة).

296
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:36,260
He said: What is Hijrah(هجرة)?

297
00:23:36,499 --> 00:23:37,626
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

298
00:23:37,782 --> 00:23:39,927
أنت هجرة ومعاصي

299
00:23:39,972 --> 00:23:41,087
 That you leave things behind.

300
00:23:41,134 --> 00:23:42,410
He said: What is the best of Hijrah(هجرة)?

301
00:23:42,752 --> 00:23:44,243
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Jihad(جهاد)!

302
00:23:44,537 --> 00:23:45,988
He said: What is the best of Jihad(جهاد)?

303
00:23:46,392 --> 00:23:49,877
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The one, whose horse is killed in his blood is spilled

304
00:23:49,929 --> 00:23:51,806
 and this is in Ahmad(أحمد), Tabrani(طبراني) and Al-Bahaqi(ألبيهقي).

305
00:23:53,650 --> 00:23:54,492
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says;

306
00:23:54,532 --> 00:23:59,140
These Ahadith(احاديث) are clear refutation of the claim that the one who wins is better than the one who is killed.

307
00:24:01,387 --> 00:24:08,386
And that's why the Muslims in the Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) three thousand in front of 200,000

308
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:15,555
which is way more than one to two or even one to ten.

309
00:24:17,591 --> 00:24:19,978
Because one to 10 would be 3000 against 30,000.

310
00:24:20,726 --> 00:24:21,954
Here we have 200,000.

311
00:24:22,024 --> 00:24:23,623
So I think it's about one to 60.

312
00:24:26,186 --> 00:24:32,723
So the Sahabah(صحابه) said: Let's wait and send Rasool Allah ﷺ consult with him.

313
00:24:32,809 --> 00:24:33,540
What should we do?

314
00:24:34,395 --> 00:24:38,076
 Either to come back or he will send some reinforcements for us

315
00:24:38,728 --> 00:24:40,719
and that's when Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) stood up

316
00:24:42,496 --> 00:24:45,044
and he just inspired the whole army.

317
00:24:45,078 --> 00:24:45,620
He said:

318
00:24:47,315 --> 00:24:53,147
You want us to run away from what we have came here, in the first place.

319
00:24:53,346 --> 00:24:57,137
The reason why we are here is to die, Shahadah(شَهَادَة) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

320
00:24:57,352 --> 00:24:59,934
And now you are you're asking us to retreat.

321
00:25:00,736 --> 00:25:05,022
So that just inspired the whole army and they decided to go ahead and would fight.

322
00:25:08,308 --> 00:25:12,292
So Shahadah(شَهَادَة) is greater than victory.

323
00:25:13,868 --> 00:25:15,610
Abdullah Bin Obaidellah Bin Umair(عبدالله بن عبيدالله بن عمير) said,

324
00:25:16,310 --> 00:25:20,911
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was circling the Ka'aba(كعبه) when he passed by a circle of men from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) sitting down.

325
00:25:21,515 --> 00:25:23,883
When they saw him they asked each other who was better,

326
00:25:24,146 --> 00:25:26,069
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) or his brother Hisham(هشام).

327
00:25:27,849 --> 00:25:30,301
When Amr(عمرو) finished his Tawaf(طواف), he walked up to them and said:

328
00:25:30,817 --> 00:25:32,808
I heard you say something about me, What was it?

329
00:25:33,492 --> 00:25:34,092
They said;

330
00:25:34,691 --> 00:25:37,876
We were wondering who's better you or your brother Hisham(هشام)?

331
00:25:38,488 --> 00:25:40,558
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: I will tell you about that.

332
00:25:41,489 --> 00:25:43,663
I was with my brother Hisham(هشام) at Yarmook(يرموك).

333
00:25:44,179 --> 00:25:48,291
And we spent our night praying that Allah blesses us with martyrdom.

334
00:25:48,894 --> 00:25:51,838
The next day my brother got it, but I didn't.

335
00:25:52,106 --> 00:25:54,228
So you can see that he was better than me.

336
00:25:55,508 --> 00:25:59,570
This is a statement from Amr(عمرو) that the one who is killed is better than the one who is not.

337
00:26:00,879 --> 00:26:01,413
12,

338
00:26:02,213 --> 00:26:07,199
the Shaheed(شَهِيد) does not feel the pain of death except like a brief sting.

339
00:26:08,083 --> 00:26:10,360
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

340
00:26:11,226 --> 00:26:13,842
The Shaheed(شَهِيد) feels nothing from the agony of death

341
00:26:13,888 --> 00:26:18,560
except like one of you would feel from a sting of an insect.

342
00:26:19,829 --> 00:26:24,069
It's in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), An-Nasai(ألنَّسائ), Ibn Majah(إبن ماجه), Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) Al-Ahmad(ألأحمد), Ad-Darimi(ألدارمي).

343
00:26:25,014 --> 00:26:27,113
In Majmo Al-Lataif(مجموع لطائف), it mentions that a man said:

344
00:26:27,173 --> 00:26:30,501
Oh Allah, take my soul without me feeling any pain.

345
00:26:31,422 --> 00:26:35,951
One day while he was walking in a farm, he felt tired, so he laid down to sleep.

346
00:26:36,717 --> 00:26:38,944
Some non believers approached him and cut off his head.

347
00:26:39,707 --> 00:26:43,336
One of his friends saw him in a dream and asked about him about himself.

348
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:46,932
He said, I slept in a farm and when I opened my eyes, I was in paradise.

349
00:26:47,602 --> 00:26:48,411
He didn't feel anything.

350
00:26:49,749 --> 00:26:53,538
Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن المبارك) mentions a similar story about two Muslim prisoners of war,

351
00:26:53,562 --> 00:26:57,022
they were threatened by the leader of the non believers to give up their religion.

352
00:26:57,451 --> 00:27:03,270
When they refused, he threw them in a container that had oil boiling for three consecutive days.

353
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:08,926
Due to the extreme heat of the oil, shortly after they were thrown in it,

354
00:27:09,244 --> 00:27:11,396
their bones stuck out from the surface.

355
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:15,790
Later on, their brother saw them in a dream and asked them about their condition.

356
00:27:16,012 --> 00:27:16,568
They said:

357
00:27:16,874 --> 00:27:23,042
It was only that first dip into the boiling oil, and then we went straight to Al-Firdaus(ألفردوس).

358
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:25,068
13,

359
00:27:26,457 --> 00:27:32,992
you see, in your dealing with Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ for example, with Ibrahim عليه السّلام and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل),

360
00:27:34,147 --> 00:27:36,282
Allah told Ibrahim عليه السّلام to slaughter his son,

361
00:27:37,019 --> 00:27:40,033
which is a very, very painful thing to do, extremely painful.

362
00:27:42,356 --> 00:27:44,185
But the whole thing was a test from Allah.

363
00:27:44,217 --> 00:27:46,388
So when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) showed the willingness to do that,

364
00:27:46,808 --> 00:27:52,896
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ not only spared him, the sacrifice of his son, but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ ransomed his son.

365
00:27:53,604 --> 00:27:59,714
And that remained as an event that we celebrate every year.

366
00:28:00,564 --> 00:28:01,328
It is a Eid(عيد).

367
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:08,977
So, the event turned into a celebration in which we would always remember Ibrahim عليه السّلام and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل).

368
00:28:10,190 --> 00:28:12,005
And that's how it is, when you're dealing with Allah,

369
00:28:12,029 --> 00:28:13,689
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not want you to suffer,

370
00:28:13,745 --> 00:28:17,042
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not want you to go through difficulty, it is just a test.

371
