558
00:42:57,650 --> 00:43:02,809
If private money is paid to free the P.O.W's and it's permission was sought.

559
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:05,958
Then he needs to pay it back after he is freed.

560
00:43:06,648 --> 00:43:08,510
If the money was paid without his knowledge,

561
00:43:08,870 --> 00:43:11,542
there is a difference of opinion whether he should pay it back or not.

562
00:43:13,473 --> 00:43:19,068
Umar Bin Abdulaziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) stated that if a Muslim P.O.W asks for Muslims to pay for his release,

563
00:43:19,578 --> 00:43:21,265
it is mandatory for Muslims to pay it.

564
00:43:22,224 --> 00:43:25,029
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says in the Tafseer(تفسير) of this verse.

565
00:43:25,705 --> 00:43:36,487
إِنَّ الَّذينَ آمَنوا وَهاجَروا وَجاهَدوا بِأَموالِهِم وَأَنفُسِهِم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ

566
00:43:37,029 --> 00:43:46,020
وَالَّذينَ آوَوا وَنَصَروا أُولٰئِكَ بَعضُهُم أَولِياءُ بَعضٍ ۚ

567
00:43:46,544 --> 00:43:57,637
وَالَّذينَ آمَنوا وَلَم يُهاجِروا ما لَكُم مِن وَلايَتِهِم مِن شَيءٍ حَتّىٰ يُهاجِروا ۚ

568
00:43:58,265 --> 00:44:04,969
وَإِنِ استَنصَروكُم فِي الدّينِ فَعَلَيكُمُ النَّصرُ إِلّا

569
00:44:05,240 --> 00:44:11,875
إِلّا عَلىٰ قَومٍ بَينَكُم وَبَينَهُم ميثاقٌ ۗ

570
00:44:12,090 --> 00:44:17,595
وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعمَلونَ بَصيرٌ۞

571
00:44:20,386 --> 00:44:26,933
But those who believed and did not immigrate for you there is no guardianship of them until they emigrated

572
00:44:26,981 --> 00:44:29,989
and if they seek help, of you for the religion then you must help,

573
00:44:30,450 --> 00:44:34,118
except against the people between yourselves and whom is a treaty.

574
00:44:34,399 --> 00:44:36,364
And Allah is Seeing of that which you do

575
00:44:36,404 --> 00:44:38,599
and this is in Al-Anfal(ألأنفال) Verse 72.

576
00:44:39,280 --> 00:44:43,244
And then he says if the believers who did not emigrate from the land of the enemy,

577
00:44:43,693 --> 00:44:48,792
asked the Muslims for help, whether in a military or financial form to release them.

578
00:44:49,256 --> 00:44:53,251
It is mandatory on the Muslims to help, and it is prohibited to forsake them.

579
00:44:53,727 --> 00:44:59,012
The only exception is if the Muslims are bound by an agreement with a non Muslim entity.

580
00:45:00,447 --> 00:45:03,956
But this only holds if the withheld Muslims are not harmed.

581
00:45:04,571 --> 00:45:06,970
If they are oppressed, then the Muslims need to help them.

582
00:45:07,679 --> 00:45:09,393
Imam Abubakr Bin Arbi(إمام أبوبكربن عربي) says,

583
00:45:09,889 --> 00:45:16,702
Except if the Muslims are oppressed in that case we need to secure their release until not a single eye among us blinks.

584
00:45:17,326 --> 00:45:19,834
 Which means, even if we all have to die for that.

585
00:45:20,917 --> 00:45:29,726
You need to fight to release that Muslim, as long as there is an eye blinking among us.

586
00:45:30,845 --> 00:45:32,228
As long as there's somebody alive.

587
00:45:33,709 --> 00:45:34,952
That's how important it is.

588
00:45:35,309 --> 00:45:39,154
And he says, it is also Qazi Abubakr Bin Arbi(قاضي أبوبكربن عربي), who said,

589
00:45:39,663 --> 00:45:48,996
if a Muslim is held captive in the West, it becomes mandatory on the Muslims to free him, even the Muslims of the east.

590
00:45:52,808 --> 00:45:56,810
These are the opinions of Imam Malik(إمام مالك) and all the other scholars.

591
00:45:57,279 --> 00:46:01,995
How unfortunate it is to see today, our brothers left in the prisons of the enemy.

592
00:46:02,583 --> 00:46:05,810
While our Treasuries are full of money, and we are full of strength.

593
00:46:06,683 --> 00:46:10,047
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is talking about his time, but it also holds true today.

594
00:46:12,877 --> 00:46:21,686
And brothers, when you're locked up in a small cell or in a cage and you speak to no one.

595
00:46:23,551 --> 00:46:26,950
And if you're married, you're far away from your wife and your children for years.

596
00:46:27,968 --> 00:46:34,087
And you just cut off from the entire world, just think how difficult that is.

597
00:46:34,772 --> 00:46:38,628
Try to lock yourself up in a room for 24 hours.

598
00:46:41,121 --> 00:46:44,850
And see how difficult it is, just the psychology psychological pain of it,

599
00:46:45,532 --> 00:46:51,322
let alone the inconvenience of the toilet facilities the food that you're eating, the temperature,

600
00:46:52,200 --> 00:46:55,011
everything else you know it's not, it's not comfortable at all.

601
00:46:58,431 --> 00:47:02,142
Umar Bin Abdulaziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) sent a letter to the Muslim POW's is in Constantinople.

602
00:47:02,640 --> 00:47:03,235
He told them!

603
00:47:04,888 --> 00:47:11,195
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) this is a Khalifah(خليفه) that had Taqwa(تقوى) and he cared for the Muslims.

604
00:47:11,234 --> 00:47:17,050
You know when he became Khalifah(خليفه).

605
00:47:17,597 --> 00:47:20,570
As soon as Baiyah(بَيْعة) was given to him when he came down from the Mimbar(ممبر).

606
00:47:20,855 --> 00:47:27,392
He sat down and he told his scribe to come and the first order that he that he gives,

607
00:47:27,987 --> 00:47:32,838
you know and some people were joking about that they said he's, he's very excited that he has became Khalifah(خليفه),

608
00:47:33,248 --> 00:47:35,508
he is so excited, he can't even wait to get to the office.

609
00:47:36,361 --> 00:47:40,253
Just came down from the Mimber(ممبر) in the Masjid(مسجد) and he is immediately, giving commands.

610
00:47:40,293 --> 00:47:47,190
The first command was, to recall the army of Muslims, that was laying siege to Constantinople.

611
00:47:48,588 --> 00:47:54,826
Even though this was a Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) against the capital of the Byzantine Empire.

612
00:47:55,601 --> 00:47:57,638
But the thing is that it was becoming personal.

613
00:47:58,412 --> 00:48:00,925
The Khalifah(خليفه) before him was becoming so stubborn about it.

614
00:48:01,983 --> 00:48:07,636
He wanted that seige to continue even though it was taken away the lives of hundreds of Muslims,

615
00:48:07,676 --> 00:48:14,419
who are dying because of hunger and cold weather, and out of stubbornness, he said carry on that siege.

616
00:48:14,807 --> 00:48:17,460
Umar Bin Abdulaziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) said: Bring that army back.

617
00:48:17,963 --> 00:48:19,510
Why are the Muslims killing themselves.?

618
00:48:20,019 --> 00:48:21,212
So he calls that army back.

619
00:48:21,292 --> 00:48:28,063
So Umar Bin Abdulaziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) had this feeling for the Muslims, he would feel for the Muslim on the street, man or woman.

620
00:48:29,001 --> 00:48:33,033
He sent this letter to the Muslim prisoners of war in Constantinople.

621
00:48:34,109 --> 00:48:41,081
He told them you consider yourselves to be prisoners of war, you are not, you are locked in the Cause of Allah,

622
00:48:41,194 --> 00:48:43,138
you are locked in cause of Allah.

623
00:48:45,726 --> 00:48:52,065
I would like you to know that what whenever I give something to the Muslims I give more to your families.

624
00:48:52,701 --> 00:48:56,889
And I'm sending so and so with five dinars for each one of you.

625
00:48:57,524 --> 00:49:01,624
And if it wasn't that I fear the Roman dictator would take it from you.

626
00:49:01,869 --> 00:49:02,803
I would have sent the more,

627
00:49:03,405 --> 00:49:10,421
I have also sent so and so to secure the release of every single one of you, regardless of what the cost would be.

628
00:49:10,752 --> 00:49:12,586
So rejoice and Assalam-O-Alaikum.

629
00:49:13,906 --> 00:49:16,072
That's how he cared for his subjects.

630
00:49:16,138 --> 00:49:18,909
Whatever it takes to free I'm going to pay.

631
00:49:19,716 --> 00:49:22,464
And now Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), I don't know if I mentioned to you this story or not

632
00:49:22,544 --> 00:49:31,051
one of my relatives told me about in another town in Yemen, he used to live there.

633
00:49:31,903 --> 00:49:36,646
He said: He personally knows, wives of some of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء),

634
00:49:38,155 --> 00:49:44,376
who would go begging from door to door begging for clothes for their children,

635
00:49:45,427 --> 00:49:48,198
 second hand clothes for them to put on Eid(عيد).

636
00:49:50,231 --> 00:49:52,952
He personally knows that he's not talking about something he heard,

637
00:49:53,032 --> 00:49:58,173
he said he knows these wives of Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) widows, they would go knocking on the doors,

638
00:49:58,577 --> 00:50:01,441
begging for second hand clothes to give to their kids on Eid(عيد).

639
00:50:03,319 --> 00:50:10,400
Government is not doing anything for them, no relief organization is doing anything for them.

640
00:50:11,241 --> 00:50:12,670
And that's how we pay back,

641
00:50:12,841 --> 00:50:17,652
that's how the Ummah(امة) is paying back the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) who gave their lives for the honor of the Ummah(امة).

642
00:50:18,860 --> 00:50:23,188
 How could we go to sleep and how could we enjoy our food.

643
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:28,536
When some of the widows of Ash-Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) are begging for secondhand clothes for their children.

644
00:50:29,776 --> 00:50:35,103
And you know, brothers, think about how difficult it is, for a woman,

645
00:50:35,843 --> 00:50:41,169
an honorable woman, a woman of dignity that never would do this never would beg,

646
00:50:41,598 --> 00:50:48,569
how difficult it is to go and knock, just imagine if your wife has to go and knock on the doors of your friend's houses,

647
00:50:49,472 --> 00:50:52,648
 begging for secondhand clothes for your kids.

648
00:50:53,984 --> 00:50:56,371
So this is a betrayal, this is this is treason.

649
00:50:56,655 --> 00:50:59,775
If we allow this to happen in the Ummah(امة), while our pockets are full.

650
00:51:02,005 --> 00:51:05,809
An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) considers that the ruling on freeing the POW's

651
00:51:05,986 --> 00:51:09,289
is similar to the ruling on the enemy invading a Muslim land.

652
00:51:10,321 --> 00:51:11,313
So it becomes Fardh-Ain(فرض عين).

653
00:51:11,842 --> 00:51:15,756
In fact he considers freeing the POW's is to be more of a priority,

654
00:51:16,160 --> 00:51:20,200
because the sanctity of the Muslim soul is greater than that of the Muslim land.

655
00:51:20,881 --> 00:51:26,040
In fact Rasool Allah ﷺ says that Hurma Damma Muslim(حرمة دم المسلم) is greater in sanctity than the house of Allah.

656
00:51:30,836 --> 00:51:35,432
 An example of that is when a Muslim woman, who was a POW with the Romans,

657
00:51:36,117 --> 00:51:38,806
in Amuriya(عمورية) was slapped in the face by a Roman.

658
00:51:39,216 --> 00:51:39,893
She then said:

659
00:51:39,933 --> 00:51:41,269
وا معتصما

660
00:51:42,073 --> 00:51:44,508
Al-Motasim(ألمعتصم) was the Muslim Khalifah(خليفه), she called his name.

661
00:51:45,566 --> 00:51:50,232
When this was related to Al-Motasim(ألمعتصم) he sent an entire army to free her.

662
00:51:51,501 --> 00:51:54,676
The Crusaders took 500 Muslim POW's in Ar-Rohaa(ألروحة).

663
00:51:56,872 --> 00:52:01,887
So, the Sultan Emad-Ud-Din Zinki(سلطان عمادالدين زنكي ) conquered the town.

664
00:52:02,372 --> 00:52:04,189
I think it's Ar-Rohaa(ألروحة).

665
00:52:05,227 --> 00:52:08,093
He conquered the town and he released all of his POW's.

666
00:52:08,181 --> 00:52:10,721
When Salahudin(صلاح الدين) won against the Crusaders in Hattein(حتين),

667
00:52:11,157 --> 00:52:15,733
he released 20,000 Muslim prisoners of war from the Crusaders.

668
00:52:16,046 --> 00:52:18,308
That was the state of the Muslim Mujahideen(مجاهدين) leaders.

669
00:52:19,647 --> 00:52:23,721
They would train Muslim POW's, while taking prisoners from their enemy,

670
00:52:24,078 --> 00:52:30,121
and then many of these non-believing POW's would embraces Islam, and ended up fighting with the Muslims.

671
00:52:30,809 --> 00:52:34,507
These are the ones meant by the Messenger of Allah in his Hadith(حديث) mentioned in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

672
00:52:35,189 --> 00:52:38,290
Allah is amazed with people who enter paradise in chains.

673
00:52:39,514 --> 00:52:42,511
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that some people will enter paradise in chains.

674
00:52:45,533 --> 00:52:50,455
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: Which means that some non believers are brought in chains as POW's,

675
00:52:50,535 --> 00:52:54,802
and then they believed in Allah, so it is as if these chains brought them to Islam.

676
00:52:56,084 --> 00:52:57,925
So they were taken as prisoners of war chained.

677
00:52:58,537 --> 00:53:02,189
That was the reason that guided them to Islams,

678
00:53:02,229 --> 00:53:07,885
so on the Day of Judgment, they would be taken to Jannah(جنة) in chains, because that's how they entered into Islam.

679
00:53:09,874 --> 00:53:13,706
The next chapter is on the history of Jihad(جهاد).

680
00:53:17,996 --> 00:53:21,996
Imam Abu Abdullah Al-Halimi(إمام أبوعبدالله ألحليمي), in his book Shuab Al-Eeman(شعب الايمان) he says:

681
00:53:23,009 --> 00:53:28,330
The Prophet ﷺ had different stages with the non believers before Jihad(جهاد) was prescribed.

682
00:53:29,160 --> 00:53:35,008
It began with the revelation of recite in the Name of your Lord, Who created, Al-Alaq(ألعلق).

683
00:53:35,783 --> 00:53:36,431
Number two,

684
00:53:37,112 --> 00:53:42,052
then Allah instructed him to convey His message, Oh you covered himself arise and warn,

685
00:53:42,092 --> 00:53:44,248
يا أَيُّهَا المُدَّثِّرُ۞ قُم فَأَنذِر۞

686
00:53:44,612 --> 00:53:46,343
So now he's going through the stages of Da'wah(دعوة).

687
00:53:46,868 --> 00:53:47,458
Number three,

688
00:53:48,053 --> 00:53:55,458
when he conveyed the message and they belied him, Allah commanded him to be patient with them.

689
00:53:56,364 --> 00:53:59,418
وَاصبِر عَلىٰ ما يَقولونَ وَاهجُرهُم هَجرًا جَميلًا۞

690
00:54:00,416 --> 00:54:04,226
And be patient over what they say and avoid them with gracious avoidance.

691
00:54:05,132 --> 00:54:06,592
That is Muzamil(مزمل) Verse 10.

692
00:54:08,504 --> 00:54:11,367
Then number four,

693
00:54:12,042 --> 00:54:18,459
When a base was provided in Madina, Allah commanded the believers to make Hijrah(هجرة), from Makkah to Madina.

694
00:54:19,205 --> 00:54:28,975
وَمَن يُهاجِر في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ يَجِد فِي الأَرضِ مُراغَمًا كَثيرًا وَسَعَةً ۚ

695
00:54:29,683 --> 00:54:39,829
وَمَن يَخرُج مِن بَيتِهِ مُهاجِرًا إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ ثُمَّ يُدرِكهُ المَوتُ

696
00:54:40,454 --> 00:54:46,732
ثُمَّ يُدرِكهُ المَوتُ فَقَد وَقَعَ أَجرُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۗ

697
00:54:47,132 --> 00:54:51,227
وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفورًا رَحيمًا۞

698
00:54:51,768 --> 00:54:58,971
And whoever emigrates for the cause of Allah will find on the earth many alternative locations and abundance.

699
00:54:59,011 --> 00:55:00,120
An-Nisa(ألنساء) Verse 100.

700
00:55:01,035 --> 00:55:01,875
Number five,

701
00:55:02,998 --> 00:55:05,820
When they made Hijrah(هجرة), they were given permission to fight.

702
00:55:07,228 --> 00:55:18,459
أُذِنَ لِلَّذينَ يُقاتَلونَ بِأَنَّهُم ظُلِموا ۚ وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلىٰ نَصرِهِم لَقَديرٌ۞

703
00:55:18,841 --> 00:55:21,825
Permission to fight has been given to those who are being fought

704
00:55:21,931 --> 00:55:26,427
because they were wronged and indeed, Allah is competent to give them victory.

705
00:55:27,005 --> 00:55:27,752
Number six,

706
00:55:28,010 --> 00:55:31,060
then they were instructed to fight whoever fights them.

707
00:55:31,443 --> 00:55:38,870
وَقاتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَكُم وَلا تَعتَدوا ۚ

708
00:55:39,249 --> 00:55:43,675
إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ المُعتَدينَ۞

709
00:55:43,941 --> 00:55:48,902
Fight in the way of Allah, those who fight you, but do not transgress.

710
00:55:48,994 --> 00:55:54,702
وَقاتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَكُم وَلا تَعتَدوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ المُعتَدينَ۞

711
00:55:54,742 --> 00:55:57,043
Indeed Allah does not like the transgressors.

712
00:55:57,496 --> 00:55:59,358
And that's in Al-Baqarah(ألبقرة) Verse 190.

713
00:56:00,469 --> 00:56:01,606
Stage number seven,

714
00:56:02,579 --> 00:56:07,092
They were later on order to fight all the non believers surrounding them.

715
00:56:07,405 --> 00:56:19,174
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا قاتِلُوا الَّذينَ يَلونَكُم مِنَ الكُفّارِ وَليَجِدوا فيكُم غِلظَةً ۚ

716
00:56:19,921 --> 00:56:26,112
وَاعلَموا أَنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ المُتَّقينَ۞

717
00:56:26,568 --> 00:56:36,910
Oh you, who have believed, fight those adjacent to you of the disbelievers, and let them find in you harshness

718
00:56:37,292 --> 00:56:39,018
and know that Allah is with the righteous,

719
00:56:39,098 --> 00:56:40,652
and this is in At-Toba(التوبة) verse 123.

720
00:56:41,498 --> 00:56:46,405
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا قاتِلُوا الَّذينَ يَلونَكُم مِنَ الكُفّارِ وَليَجِدوا فيكُم غِلظَةً ۚ

721
00:56:48,145 --> 00:56:51,884
Allah told them let fighting is prescribed on them and is compulsory,

722
00:56:51,964 --> 00:56:58,209
كُتِبَ عَلَيكُمُ القِتالُ وَهُوَ كُرهٌ لَكُم ۖ وَعَسىٰ أَن تَكرَهوا شَيئًا وَهُوَ خَيرٌ لَكُم ۖ

723
00:56:58,321 --> 00:57:08,178
Oh you who have believed, Fighting has been enjoined upon you, while it is hateful to you,

724
00:57:08,515 --> 00:57:13,458
but perhaps you hate the thing, and it is good for you, and perhaps you love a thing and it's bad for you.

725
00:57:13,782 --> 00:57:15,250
And Allah knows while you know not.

726
00:57:15,872 --> 00:57:19,755
Allah also told them that fighting is a covenant between them and Allah.

727
00:57:20,720 --> 00:57:21,942
And that's the Ayah(آية),

728
00:57:21,982 --> 00:57:26,116
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

729
00:57:28,590 --> 00:57:30,558
And then he also says,

730
00:57:31,339 --> 00:57:38,050
So when Allah prescribed Jihad(جهاد), accepting it, and following it became part and its parcel of Eeman(ايمان).

731
00:57:38,645 --> 00:57:43,054
The contract is that whoever kills the non believers is rewarded with paradise

732
00:57:43,424 --> 00:57:47,293
and whomever the non believers kill is rewarded with paradise.

733
00:57:48,120 --> 00:57:52,074
You kill the non believers, you go to paradise, you are killed by the non believers you go to paradise.

734
00:57:52,845 --> 00:57:58,226
If you accept this contract, and you wanted paradise, then you must fulfill your part of the agreement,

735
00:57:58,643 --> 00:58:00,970
and that is giving your soul and wealth to Allah.

736
00:58:02,485 --> 00:58:06,920
And then he says: The value of the merchandise is dependent on three elements.

737
00:58:07,459 --> 00:58:08,458
Number one, the buyer.

738
00:58:09,470 --> 00:58:12,868
A noble buyer would only buy valuable merchandise.

739
00:58:13,564 --> 00:58:18,311
You know, what is the most expensive shopping center in this country?

740
00:58:20,718 --> 00:58:23,665
 Harrods.

741
00:58:24,331 --> 00:58:27,001
There's a dissenting view over here.

742
00:58:29,027 --> 00:58:29,644
Okay Harrods.

743
00:58:30,179 --> 00:58:32,752
When you go to Harrods, do you find homeless people shopping.?

744
00:58:33,592 --> 00:58:40,059
 Do you find the rank and file shopping or you would find the high class shopping in Harrods.

745
00:58:40,423 --> 00:58:49,675
So, the nobel buyers and the wealthy, they would only buy valuable stuff, stuff has to have value.

746
00:58:50,939 --> 00:58:52,244
Number two the salesman.

747
00:58:52,584 --> 00:58:57,271
A noble salesman would not negotiate an invaluable sale.

748
00:58:58,531 --> 00:59:03,535
Noble salesman will not negotiate an invaluable sale.

749
00:59:06,155 --> 00:59:08,395
The salesman will only look for what is worthy.

750
00:59:08,977 --> 00:59:09,990
Number three, the price,

751
00:59:10,387 --> 00:59:13,814
an expensive price is not paid for worthless merchandise.

752
00:59:13,854 --> 00:59:17,692
I cannot sell you this cookie for 100 pounds,

753
00:59:19,136 --> 00:59:22,467
but I can sell you this mini disc player for 100 pounds.

754
00:59:23,479 --> 00:59:26,144
So there needs to be some value.

755
00:59:27,358 --> 00:59:28,533
So what is the item.?

756
00:59:29,133 --> 00:59:30,390
It says the believer's soul,

757
00:59:31,229 --> 00:59:31,924
so that's the item,

758
00:59:32,413 --> 00:59:34,734
look at the value of Allah put on your soul.

759
00:59:35,226 --> 00:59:36,020
 He is the buyer.

760
00:59:37,634 --> 00:59:39,421
Muhammadﷺ is the salesman,

761
00:59:40,962 --> 00:59:42,811
and the price is paradise.

762
00:59:44,431 --> 00:59:46,964
That is the greatest honor for the believers.

763
00:59:47,760 --> 00:59:51,095
The only condition Allah placed on receiving the price, paradise

764
00:59:51,433 --> 00:59:55,512
is for you to fight in the cause of Allah with your soul, and your wealth.

765
00:59:57,087 --> 01:00:00,776
They fight in the Cause of Allah so they kill, and are killed.

766
01:00:01,973 --> 01:00:05,194
Allah even recorded the contract for you a true promise,

767
01:00:05,280 --> 01:00:09,559
the contract is recorded in the three books, Qur'an, Torah(توراة) and Injeel(أنجيل).

768
01:00:10,194 --> 01:00:10,967
Allah says:

769
01:00:11,979 --> 01:00:19,979
A true promise binding upon him in the Torah(توراة) and the Gospel and Qur'an.

770
01:00:20,681 --> 01:00:26,378
So, the contract is not documented once, but there are three documents, Al-Quran(ألقرآن), gospel and Torah(توراة).

771
01:00:27,758 --> 01:00:32,557
 Scholars differed on the exact number of battles, the Messenger of Allah, went out.

772
01:00:32,664 --> 01:00:36,751
In Muslim(ألمسلم) Jabir(جابر) states, the Messenger of Allah fought in 21 battles.

773
01:00:37,247 --> 01:00:42,241
Zaid(زيد) mentions 19, while Ibn Is'haq(إبن إسحاق) mentioned, 27.

774
01:00:42,988 --> 01:00:46,391
You have in Seerah(سيرة) something called Ghazwa(غزوة), and you have something called Sariyah(سرية).

775
01:00:46,847 --> 01:00:47,978
What's the difference between the two.?

776
01:00:48,798 --> 01:00:50,108
There's Ghazwa(غزوة) and there's Sariyah(سرية).

777
01:00:52,138 --> 01:00:56,554
Linguistically Ghazwa(غزوة) means to attack or raid, that is Ghazwa(غزوة).

778
01:00:57,092 --> 01:00:59,240
And Sariyah(سرية) means detachment.

779
01:01:01,105 --> 01:01:03,633
So what's the difference between the two? Ghazwa(غزوة) and Sariyah(سرية).

780
01:01:06,010 --> 01:01:07,010
Yes

781
01:01:14,717 --> 01:01:15,716
Okay, which one is which.

782
01:01:20,209 --> 01:01:22,304
Okay, Ghazwa(غزوة) is the one Rasool Allah ﷺ went with.

783
01:01:23,356 --> 01:01:25,453
Do we call Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) Ghazwa(غزوة) or Sariyah(سرية)?

784
01:01:29,782 --> 01:01:31,695
You need to answer that

785
01:01:34,499 --> 01:01:35,553
No it's called Ghazwa(غزوة)

786
01:01:41,532 --> 01:01:43,639
The answer is right!

787
01:01:43,684 --> 01:01:46,222
Ghazwa(غزوة) is when Rasool Allah ﷺ goes out is called Ghazwa(غزوة)

788
01:01:46,569 --> 01:01:47,942
and Sariyah(سرية) when he doesn't go out.

789
01:01:48,209 --> 01:01:51,009
But how come Ghazwa Mu'tah(غزوة مَؤتَة) is called Ghazwa(غزوة) when Rasool Ullah didn't go out?

790
01:01:54,758 --> 01:01:55,417
No!

791
01:01:58,603 --> 01:01:59,027
Alright!

792
01:01:59,092 --> 01:01:59,853
this was, yes!

793
01:02:03,498 --> 01:02:09,790
That was Usama Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد)'s one, which was a consequence of the Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

794
01:02:11,665 --> 01:02:14,463
The reason why Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) is called Ghazwa(غزوة), is because

795
01:02:15,667 --> 01:02:17,701
it's given this title as an exception is because,

796
01:02:17,741 --> 01:02:23,491
Ghazwa Mu'tah(غزوة مَؤتَة), was such a great and important event so it was elevated to the status a Ghazwa(غزوة).

797
01:02:23,943 --> 01:02:28,586
 That's the reason, it was elevated to a status of as Ghazwa(غزوة), because of the importance of it.

798
01:02:29,161 --> 01:02:33,416
This was the first confrontation between the Muslims and Ahlal Al-Kitab(أهل الكتاب) Ar-Rome(أللروم),

799
01:02:33,956 --> 01:02:39,971
 and it was a large army of 3000 and great events happen there in.

800
01:02:40,051 --> 01:02:44,881
So, it is referred to in all of the books of history as a Ghazwa(غزوة) and not as Sariyah(سرية).

801
01:02:45,829 --> 01:02:49,579
Sariyah(سرية) is tends to be smaller in size.

802
01:02:50,296 --> 01:03:03,535
And mostly they were raiding armies led by Sahabah رضي الله عنهم as part of the economical warfare, led by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

803
01:03:04,078 --> 01:03:06,668
While that Ghazwaat(غزوات), In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله) we'll go through them

804
01:03:06,708 --> 01:03:10,710
and we'll just then read a list of the Sarayah(سراية) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

805
01:03:11,814 --> 01:03:13,185
Number one, Al-Abwa(ألأبواء),

806
01:03:13,364 --> 01:03:17,848
and there's not enough time to go through every one of them

807
01:03:17,914 --> 01:03:21,666
in fact, Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) himself doesn't really elaborate much on them.

808
01:03:22,405 --> 01:03:24,369
Sometimes he just mentions, the title of the Ghazwa(غزوة).

809
01:03:25,156 --> 01:03:30,375
But Al-Abwa(ألأبواء) number one, this occurred in Safar(صفر), in the first year of Hijrah(هجرة) and no fighting occurred.

810
01:03:31,016 --> 01:03:34,899
 Number two Buaat(بوات), this happened in Rabi-Ul-Awal(ربيع الأول), second year of Hijrah(هجرة).

811
01:03:35,745 --> 01:03:42,443
Number three, Al-Asheerah(ألعشيرة), and this happened in Jumada Al-Ula(جمادى ألأولى) second year of Hijrah.

812
01:03:42,896 --> 01:03:46,906
And then you have the first battle of Badr(بدر) and this occurred a few days after Al-Asheerah(ألعشيرة).

813
01:03:47,506 --> 01:03:49,201
And then you have the major battle of Badr(بدر),

814
01:03:49,388 --> 01:03:55,389
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says this was the great battle which honored Islam and humiliated the infidels.

815
01:03:59,138 --> 01:04:01,459
It was one of the greatest days for the Muslims.

816
01:04:01,836 --> 01:04:07,687
It occurred, the morning of the 17th of Ramadan(رمضان), second year of Hijrah(هجرة).

817
01:04:09,116 --> 01:04:11,247
So this was one of the battles of Ramadan(رمضان),

818
01:04:12,246 --> 01:04:16,505
by the way the month of Ramadan(رمضان) is the month of Jihad(جهاد), that's when Badr(بدر) occurred,

819
01:04:17,272 --> 01:04:19,251
Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه), Ain-Jalut(عين جالوت).

820
01:04:21,090 --> 01:04:24,658
A little over 310 Sahabah(صحابه) participated in it.

821
01:04:26,477 --> 01:04:31,963
And Wallah Ho Alam(ولله أعلم) the number of Sahabah(صحابه) who participate in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

822
01:04:32,373 --> 01:04:35,441
is the same number of fighters that fight with Talut(طالوت).

823
01:04:38,046 --> 01:04:42,004
Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) said: The Sahabah(صحابه), of the Messenger of Allah told me

824
01:04:42,372 --> 01:04:47,832
that the number of Muslims in the Battle of Badr(بدر) was the same number of fighters in the army of Talut(طالوت).

825
01:04:48,709 --> 01:04:50,766
Now the enemy was 1000 strong.

826
01:04:51,818 --> 01:04:57,343
When Rasool Allah ﷺ heard of the caravan carrying a huge amount of wealth, belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

827
01:04:57,779 --> 01:04:59,694
He encourages his Sahabah(صحابه) to confiscate it.

828
01:05:00,302 --> 01:05:05,214
They missed the caravan but ended up meeting an army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) that rushed to the defense of the caravan.

829
01:05:06,135 --> 01:05:10,309
The battle started with three men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) fighting one on one

830
01:05:10,650 --> 01:05:14,968
 with Hamza(حمزه), Ali(علي), and Ubaidah Bin Haris(عبيدة بن حارث).

831
01:05:15,592 --> 01:05:17,316
All three men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were killed.

832
01:05:17,462 --> 01:05:20,476
Rasool Allah ﷺ then straighten the ranks of the army.

833
01:05:20,992 --> 01:05:24,187
He was walking in front of the ranks with a piece of wood in his hand.

834
01:05:24,729 --> 01:05:33,753
Rasool Allah ﷺ was straightening the ranks, wanted the ranks to be straight, and nobody protruding out of these ranks.

835
01:05:34,573 --> 01:05:35,856
 Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

836
01:05:35,896 --> 01:05:40,132
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ۞

837
01:05:40,473 --> 01:05:43,502
As if they are, Bunyaan Marsoos(بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ), as if they are a wall.

838
01:05:44,874 --> 01:05:50,726
So, Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyyah(سوادبن غزية) one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم was a step ahead of the rest.

839
01:05:51,169 --> 01:05:54,247
So Rasool Allah ﷺ pushed him in the stomach and told him,

840
01:05:54,287 --> 01:05:55,190
إستو يا سواد

841
01:05:56,245 --> 01:05:58,441
Sawad(سواد) said: O Rasool Allah ﷺ you hurt me.

842
01:05:59,373 --> 01:06:04,250
So I want to, to get even with you.

843
01:06:05,773 --> 01:06:07,244
Just imagine the Sahabah(صحابه) hearing that,

844
01:06:09,142 --> 01:06:11,177
he want to get even with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

845
01:06:12,640 --> 01:06:14,806
But Rasool Allah ﷺ very calmly, he said:

846
01:06:15,401 --> 01:06:19,026
Go ahead and he uncovered his stomach Rasul Ullah uncovered his stomach for Sawad(سواد).

847
01:06:20,699 --> 01:06:24,701
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the leader, the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah, he could have disciplined Sawad(سواد)

848
01:06:25,860 --> 01:06:28,192
asking to get even with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

849
01:06:30,428 --> 01:06:35,227
And then Sawad(سواد), he just jumped on Rasool Allah ﷺ hugged him and kissed his stomach.

850
01:06:36,834 --> 01:06:37,876
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

851
01:06:37,916 --> 01:06:39,787
يا سواد ما حملك على ما صنعتك

852
01:06:39,867 --> 01:06:41,293
O sawad(سواد), why did he do that.

853
01:06:42,347 --> 01:06:42,605
He said:

854
01:06:42,671 --> 01:06:44,657
لقد حضر ما ترى من القتال

855
01:06:45,140 --> 01:06:50,937
O messenger of Allah you see what we are going to face and this might be the last day in my life.

856
01:06:51,618 --> 01:06:56,123
So I wanted my last moments to be my skin, touching yours.

857
01:06:57,517 --> 01:07:00,709
I wanted my last moments to be my skin, touching yours.

858
01:07:01,542 --> 01:07:04,710
That's the whole point why he wanted to get even with the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

859
01:07:05,153 --> 01:07:06,739
So, that he could hug it Rasul Ullah and kiss him,

860
01:07:07,248 --> 01:07:10,674
Rasool Allah ﷺ went aside and started supplicating, he said:

861
01:07:10,740 --> 01:07:15,458
Oh Allah, if you allow this band to be destroyed, you won't be worshipped after this day.

862
01:07:16,750 --> 01:07:21,202
There are no Muslims on the face of the earth except these, if they die, you are not going to be worshipped.

863
01:07:23,546 --> 01:07:28,357
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Enough of asking Allah, Allah has promised you and will fulfill His promise.

864
01:07:29,193 --> 01:07:32,180
Rasool Allah ﷺ a little later said: Rejoice, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)!

865
01:07:32,314 --> 01:07:33,499
أبشر يا أبا بكر

866
01:07:34,543 --> 01:07:36,258
The victory of Allah is near.

867
01:07:37,107 --> 01:07:39,382
Here comes Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), riding his horse.

868
01:07:41,245 --> 01:07:42,600
 Allah says about that day:

869
01:07:42,826 --> 01:07:51,770
إِذ يوحي رَبُّكَ إِلَى المَلائِكَةِ أَنّي مَعَكُم فَثَبِّتُوا الَّذينَ آمَنوا ۚ

870
01:07:52,135 --> 01:08:02,260
سَأُلقي في قُلوبِ الَّذينَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعبَ فَاضرِبوا فَوقَ الأَعناقِ وَاضرِبوا مِنهُم كُلَّ بَنانٍ۞

871
01:08:02,729 --> 01:08:09,016
Remember when your Lord inspired his angels, I am with you, so strengthen those who have believed,

872
01:08:09,764 --> 01:08:13,316
I will cast her into the hearts of those who disbelieved,

873
01:08:13,975 --> 01:08:18,180
so strike upon the necks and strike from them every fingertip.

874
01:08:18,419 --> 01:08:20,613
This is in Al-Anfal(أنفال) Verse 12.

875
01:08:20,735 --> 01:08:21,901
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

876
01:08:24,935 --> 01:08:35,124
إِذ يوحي رَبُّكَ إِلَى المَلائِكَةِ أَنّي مَعَكُم فَثَبِّتُوا الَّذينَ آمَنوا ۚ سَأُلقي في قُلوبِ الَّذينَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعبَ

877
01:08:35,375 --> 01:08:40,400
 فَاضرِبوا فَوقَ الأَعناقِ وَاضرِبوا مِنهُم كُلَّ بَنانٍ۞

878
01:08:41,402 --> 01:08:45,882
Strike on their necks, strike their fingertips, which are holding the swords.

879
01:08:47,158 --> 01:08:50,852
The battle was joined by 5000 Angels led by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) himself.

880
01:08:52,354 --> 01:08:55,480
Rifa'a(رفاعة) narrated Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) came to the Messenger of Allah and told him.

881
01:08:55,877 --> 01:08:58,001
What do you consider the people of Badr(بدر) to be among you?

882
01:08:58,087 --> 01:09:00,167
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We considered them to be the best.

883
01:09:00,693 --> 01:09:01,426
 Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said;

884
01:09:01,963 --> 01:09:06,516
And so we the angels consider the angels who attended Badr(بدر) to be the best among us.

885
01:09:07,052 --> 01:09:10,935
So Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) wasn't only in an event of this world but it was a universal event.

886
01:09:13,310 --> 01:09:16,418
The best of angels are the angels who attended the Battle of Badr(بدر),

887
01:09:16,737 --> 01:09:20,365
so it is an event that is witnessed by the creation of the heavens

888
01:09:20,405 --> 01:09:22,081
because, you know,

889
01:09:22,991 --> 01:09:28,282
if you go and read the encyclopedias of war of the history of the world you might not come across the Battle of the Badr(بدر).

890
01:09:29,124 --> 01:09:32,365
Kuffar(كفار), they don't even know what Badr(بدر) is, but that doesn't really mean anything.

891
01:09:33,335 --> 01:09:35,083
But the angels know what Badr(بدر) is.

892
01:09:35,895 --> 01:09:39,870
And the classification of the angels is based on the participation of Badr(بدر).

893
01:09:40,865 --> 01:09:49,047
So it was an event that was witnessed by As-Saliheen(ألصالحين), and by the angels, and by a Shayateen(شياطين),

894
01:09:49,353 --> 01:09:51,813
they were very displeased with the results.

895
01:09:53,919 --> 01:09:58,008
70 of the infidels were killed and 70 were taken prisoners.

896
01:09:58,376 --> 01:09:59,188
Allah says:

897
01:09:59,334 --> 01:10:05,344
وَلَقَد نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِبَدرٍ وَأَنتُم أَذِلَّةٌ ۖ

898
01:10:05,634 --> 01:10:10,003
فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُم تَشكُرونَ۞

899
01:10:10,577 --> 01:10:16,024
And already had Allah, given you victory at Badr(بدر) while you were weak.

900
01:10:18,912 --> 01:10:21,047
Then fear Allah, perhaps you would be grateful.

901
01:10:21,374 --> 01:10:23,145
Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 123.

902
01:10:25,752 --> 01:10:27,856
Number six, Banu Sulaim(بنوسُلَيم).

903
01:10:29,046 --> 01:10:34,812
Seven days after returning from Badr(بدر) Rasool Allah ﷺ attacked Banu Sulaim(بنوسُلَيم), but no fighting occurred.

904
01:10:35,200 --> 01:10:38,310
He camped in their land for three days and then returned to Madina.

905
01:10:38,433 --> 01:10:39,012
Number seven,

906
01:10:39,434 --> 01:10:40,565
Banu Qainqah(بنوقينقاع),

907
01:10:41,583 --> 01:10:44,624
Banu Qainqah(بنوقينقاع) is the first conflict between the Muslims and the Jews.

908
01:10:45,118 --> 01:10:51,024
Rasool Allah ﷺ, after the Battle of Badr(بدر) went to the Jews in their marketplace.

909
01:10:53,020 --> 01:10:58,529
And he said: You know that I'm the Messenger of Allah so follow me.

910
01:10:59,365 --> 01:11:02,230
Otherwise the fate of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) will befall you.

911
01:11:03,742 --> 01:11:04,955
What did Banu Qainqah(بنوقينقاع) say?

912
01:11:06,002 --> 01:11:13,134
They said: Don't boast about that victory because you have met people who have no experience in fighting.

913
01:11:13,928 --> 01:11:15,895
If you meet us, you'll know who the real men are.

914
